{% comment %}
  Advertorial lede — the opening argument, split around a single large statistic.

  The stat sits between the two prose blocks on mobile (a rule-bounded band in the
  reading flow) and moves to a sticky right-hand rail on desktop. Both come from the
  same markup via explicit grid placement, so the copy stays in one reading order.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="adv adv-lede adv-section">
  <div class="adv-lede__inner adv-container">
    <div class="adv-lede__copy adv-lede__copy--a">
      {%- if section.settings.lead != blank -%}
        <p class="adv-lead">{{ section.settings.lead }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.body_before != blank -%}
        <div class="adv-prose">{{ section.settings.body_before }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.stat_value != blank -%}
      <div class="adv-lede__stat">
        <span class="adv-lede__stat-value">
          {{- section.settings.stat_value -}}
          {%- if section.settings.stat_unit != blank -%}
            <span class="adv-lede__stat-unit">{{ section.settings.stat_unit }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- if section.settings.stat_label != blank -%}
          <span class="adv-lede__stat-label">{{ section.settings.stat_label }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.body_after != blank -%}
      <div class="adv-lede__copy adv-lede__copy--b">
        <div class="adv-prose">{{ section.settings.body_after }}</div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .adv-lede__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .adv-lede__copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
  }

  /* Mobile: rule-bounded band sitting in the reading flow. */
  .adv-lede__stat {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 0 16px;
    align-items: center;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--retaur-black);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--retaur-black);
    padding: 18px 0;
    margin: 4px 0;
  }

  .adv-lede__stat-value {
    font-size: 48px;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 0.9;
    color: var(--retaur-black);
  }

  .adv-lede__stat-unit {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .adv-lede__stat-label {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--adv-ink-soft);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .adv-lede__inner {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(300px, 1fr);
      column-gap: 80px;
      row-gap: 22px;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .adv-lede__copy {
      gap: 22px;
    }

    .adv-lede__copy--a {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 1;
    }

    .adv-lede__copy--b {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 2;
    }

    /* Rail: spans both copy rows so it can stick alongside the whole argument. */
    .adv-lede__stat {
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 1 / span 2;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 14px;
      border-top: 3px solid var(--retaur-black);
      border-bottom: 0;
      padding: 24px 0 0;
      margin: 0;
      position: sticky;
      top: 120px;
    }

    .adv-lede__stat-value {
      font-size: 96px;
      letter-spacing: -0.055em;
      line-height: 0.85;
    }

    .adv-lede__stat-unit {
      font-size: 36px;
    }

    .adv-lede__stat-label {
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.4;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      max-width: 16em;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Advertorial lede",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "adv-lede-section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["page"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "lead",
      "label": "Opening line",
      "default": "You made the right decision already."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body_before",
      "label": "Copy above the statistic",
      "default": "<p>You skipped the sugary drinking yogurts. You went to the shelf with the thick Greek-style cups, the ones with the clean packaging and the word Greek on the front, and you paid ₦5,500 for one because you're trying to eat more protein and this seemed like the sensible way to do it.</p><p>That was a good call. It's just that you're getting less for it than you think.</p><p>Turn the cup around. Find the nutrition panel. Look at protein per 100g.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Statistic"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "stat_value",
      "label": "Value",
      "default": "8 to 10"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "stat_unit",
      "label": "Unit",
      "info": "Set smaller than the value, e.g. the g in 10g.",
      "default": "g"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "stat_label",
      "label": "Label",
      "default": "Protein per 100g on most cups on that shelf"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Copy below the statistic"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body_after",
      "label": "Copy",
      "default": "<p>On a 400g cup, that's <strong>30 to 40 grams of protein</strong> for your ₦5,500.</p><p>Which is fine. It's just not what you're paying for.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Advertorial lede"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
